X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unioncong": "https://www.unioncong.org/event/bethlehem-free-trade-artisans-sale-after-worship/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unioncong
X-SOURCE:Union Congregational Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260607T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260607T120000
DTSTAMP:20260606T001000
CREATED:20260604T201128Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260604T211136Z
UID:10004225-1780830000-1780833600@www.unioncong.org
SUMMARY:Bethlehem Fair Trade Artisans Sale After Worship
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in the Assembly Room on Sunday\, June 7th after worship for a sale of select items handcrafted by the Bethlehem Fair Trade Artisans (BFTA)\, including sandals and olive wood creches\, keepsake boxes\, and cheeseboards.  BFTA (https://bethlehemfairtrade.org/) is a non-profit NGO\, established in 2009\, that aims to improve the lives of Palestians by connecting marginalized Palestinian artisans – mostly women – with a larger market for their products. Their work is essential to the life of the community\, especially in the wake of settler violence which has cut off the tourist trade and other sources of income. \nThe suggested donation for each item reflects a deep discount. You are also welcome to donate what you wish. You can pay with cash or use the QR code available at our table. \nOther items\, including textiles\, glass\, ceramics\, pottery\, and soaps can be purchased directly through BFTA’s website: https://bethlehemfairtrade.org/
URL:https://www.unioncong.org/event/bethlehem-free-trade-artisans-sale-after-worship/
LOCATION:Assembly Room
CATEGORIES:All Church Events,All Events,Featured Events,Justice & Community Engagement
END:VEVENT
