DTSTART:20260614T180000Z
DTEND:20260614T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260614T000000Z
SUMMARY:Jazz film screening - Billy Bang: Lucky Man
DESCRIPTION:In March 1967\, BILLY BANG was conscripted to fight one year in 
 the jungles of Vietnam\, an experience that left him emotionally desolate 
 and profoundly confused about his American identity. Upon his return\, he 
 tried to forget his nightmares through alcohol\, drugs and music.\n\nForty 
 years later\, he decides that the only way to repair his emotions and find 
 closure to his trauma was to return to Vietnam\, this time with his 
 violin.‍ Billy Bang: Lucky Man documents his brave return to the 
 battlefields of his past\, fraught with memories and flashbacks\, in 
 contrast to the ebullient and youthful Vietnam of today as he encountered a 
 people and a culture that he had never known\, and had been taught to 
 hate.\n\nBang's journey takes him through the rich musical traditions of 
 Vietnam\, from Saigon and the Mekong Delta\, north across the 17th 
 parallel\, climaxing with his collaboration with the Hanoi symphony 
 orchestra.‍ Billy Bang: Lucky Man is about his desire to overcome and 
 transcend the trauma of war through music and art.\n\n________\n\n“Billy 
 Bang Lucky Man\,' which documented Billy Bang's return to Vietnam\, blew me 
 away away. There were no punches pulled as we got to see this former GI - 
 "a tunnel rat" - deal simultaneously with the people he once viewed and 
 treated as the enemy while negotiating his own trauma and emotional 
 turmoil. This film boldly documents the musical redemption\, the journey to 
 the light\, that Billy Bang experienced as a result of that trip to the 
 heart of darkness.”\nPaul Bradshaw - Straight No Chaser
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10306-16269376
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16269376
END:VEVENT
